    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Bryson Stott** (69.25) stands as our premier offensive anchor. His matchup against Cecconi is ideal; the combination of a favorable platoon advantage and a slow opposing delivery maximizes his upside in our scarcity-focused 5x5 format. He is joined in the top-tier of our daily output by **Masyn Winn** (64.02), who benefits from a high-run-environment matchup against Petty (6.50 xERA), and **Tyler Freeman** (62.30), whose placement in the clean-up spot against a neutral-matched Gallen provides a solid floor for RBI opportunities. **Will Smith** and **Geraldo Perdomo** also grade out as strong starts, as both leverage favorable park factors and mid-tier opposing arms to secure scores safely above our 60.00 threshold.\n\nConversely, our lineup construction faces significant resistance from elite arms like Wheeler and Skenes, which drags down the projected value for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (54.81) and **Daulton Varsho** (50.42). While their raw talent prevents them from being benched, we are bracing for limited production in those specific slots. The tightest decision of the day involved the bottom of the order, where **Drew Gilbert** (41.40) barely edged out our depth options; he is essentially a placeholder today, as his L/L platoon disadvantage and position in the nine-hole create significant volatility. We remain cautious regarding **Taylor Ward**, who is unavailable due to a rainout, and we continue to monitor the IL status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, both of whom are essential to our long-term health once they clear their respective medical hurdles. **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** also offer marginal utility today; while they aren't the primary drivers of our stolen base hunt, their ability to navigate mid-range matchups keeps them ahead of bench assets like **Lawrence Butler** or **Jonathan Aranda** in our current optimization framework.",
